From b734ddf33a40ddb7f6bebfb72fd10bb1d69dc195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:48:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 95/96] video: rockchip: rga3: harden request and DMA-BUF
 ownership

Canonicalize every high-address RGA2 DMA-BUF through a bounded job-shared DMA32 staging object so aliases share one image even when a direct SWIOTLB mapping would succeed. Copy staged output back once only after successful quiesced completion, and account job, session, and global staging limits.

Make imported handles session-authorized and transactional, close duplicate-import and diagnostic lifetime races, balance runtime-PM and pre-start unwind paths, and serialize request configuration, execution, cancellation, completion, fence callbacks, and shutdown. Reusable MPI contexts now retain one explicit owner and one run at a time; scheduler shutdown drains all work even if hardware cannot be resumed.
